SIROM — authorship and copyright

Copyright (c) 2020-2026 Renan Brito Cano Butkeraites

All commits in this repository were authored by Renan Brito Cano Butkeraites.
Four git identities appear in the history because the configured address
changed over the years; they are all the same person:

    renan@fresh-codes.com
    rbritobut@gmail.com
    rbritobut?@gmail.com          (malformed; holds the initial commit)
    renan.butkeraites@nitryx.com

A fifth identity, dependabot[bot], appears on dependency-bump commits that
carry no copyrightable expression.

The commit that relicensed this project from GPL-3.0 to MIT gave the count as
"104 commits" across three identities. Both figures were wrong: the history
holds roughly 124 human commits across the four identities listed above. This
file is the correct record; the commit message cannot be edited without
rewriting published history.

SCOPE OF THE MIT LICENCE

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the source code in this repository.

It conveys no rights in the paper that describes the method:

    R. B. C. Butkeraites, L. L. de Salles Neto and M. Gendreau,
    "A sampling-based multi-objective iterative robust optimization method
    for the Bandwidth Packing Problem", Expert Systems with Applications,
    203:117337, 2022. doi:10.1016/j.eswa.2022.117337

That paper is copyright its publisher and is co-authored with two people who
are not parties to this licence. Cite the paper; the code is MIT.
